 #1c1b16;padding:14px 44px 26px;"><p class="e-faint" style="color:#65635e;margin:0;font:11px/17px Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;">Ferrer Arquitectura · C/ de Mar 41, 08911 Badalona<br>You get this as an agent on the project. <a href="https://www.ifcvieweronline.eu/u/abc" class="e-faint" style="color:#65635e;text-decoration:underline;">Unsubscribe</a></p></td></tr></table><!--[if mso]></td></tr></table><![endif]--></td></tr></table></body></html>"`;

exports[`editorial templates > rfi > en: plain text snapshot 1`] = `
"LLEVANT 84 · No. 23 · 13 Nov 2026
BIM coordination bulletin · Llevant Residential · 84 homes
For: Procurement and site management · From: Marta Vidal

OPENINGS IN THE BEAMS, OR DRAINAGE BELOW THEM?

Beams V-PB-12 to V-PB-17 cross the collector route. Structure accepts openings up to Ø160 with reinforcement. The alternative lowers the car-park ceiling by 25 cm.
— Marta Vidal, BIM Coordinator · Ferrer Arquitectura
Which solution do we ask Instal·lacions Garraf and Estructuras EGS for?
  A) Ø160 sleeved openings with reinforcement in 6 beams — +€3,100 · no delay · structure reviews on 18 Nov
  B) Collector below the beams — +€7,300 · ceiling at 2.25 m · 5 more days of services work
Decide by Tue 18 Nov · Jordi Puig, site manager
[GF · grid C–D / 2–4 · affected beams in orange]
Open this view: https://www.ifcvieweronline.eu/?v=llv-rfi031
Coordination recommendation: option A. It is cheaper, keeps the car-park clearance, and structure has already checked it in preliminary calculation.

Answer the RFI: https://www.ifcvieweronline.eu/?rfi=031

—
Project: Llevant Residential · 84 homes · Phase: Detailed design · Rev. P05
Author: Marta Vidal · Ferrer Arquitectura · Date: 13 Nov 2026 · Code: LLV-FER-ZZ-XX-RP-B-0023
Ferrer Arquitectura · C/ de Mar 41, 08911 Badalona
You get this as an agent on the project. Unsubscribe: https://www.ifcvieweronline.eu/u/abc
"
`;

